Expected elements: present

Identity bar (exit to the chain, both step directions, scrubber, readout, phase rail), Code positioned on line 32, Call Trace + Event Log as one tabbed region with Call Trace open, Values as a separate pane below it, and the `Data` provenance row inside the transaction pane are all present. No provenance band, no prose band, no full-width pane, no spinner. The register still reads as the desktop tool.

(a), (b) and (c) all landed. The EXECUTIONS note is now a punctuated sentence; the decoded-input note names BlockTracer as the holder and that subject is right — the sentence is about what the holder cannot know; the em dash is the correct table convention and declining "None published" was the honest call. (c) exposed something it did not cause: with `0x` gone, the label `RAW` collides with `RAW (CHAIN-NATIVE)` 130px below, and both wear the same caps style as the group headers `DECODED INPUT` and `EXECUTIONS`, so one label primitive serves two structural levels.

Re-filing (d) plainly: `Status reason: private-part-succeeded-public-part-succeeded` is still a raw enum given an English label, wrapping two lines, two rows above the badge that claims to say what this data is. It is a defect.

Fresh: the Code pane's elision notice is set in the code face at code size and ends "not in this window" — UI prose typeset as program text, using the virtual-scroll noun.

Fix first: the code-pane notice; then the status-reason enum.

Rating: 6/10

